# Architecture & Performance

## SOLID

- Screens and UI components stay declarative. Put business logic, API calls, and mutations in `lib/*-store`, `lib/api.ts`, or `hooks/`.
- One responsibility per module. Do not grow route files into god screens.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — fetch inside a screen
useEffect(() => { fetch(url).then(r => r.json()).then(setRoom); }, []);

// ✅ GOOD — store owns I/O; screen subscribes
useEffect(() => subscribeSession(() => setSession(getSession())), []);
```

## Performance

- Avoid extra re-renders: stable callbacks (`useCallback`) only when passed to memoized children; proper `key`s in lists.
- Large lists: `FlatList` (tuned `keyExtractor`, avoid heavy items). Do not map long datasets inside a `ScrollView`. Do not add FlashList unless already a dependency and needed.
- Animations: Reanimated / native driver. Keep motion subtle; haptics on decisive actions (Oui / Passer) when available.
- Polling: only via `hooks/use-polling.ts`, focused + `AppState` active, never a global interval. Enable only in lobby / `waiting_partner`.
- Guard async UI after unmount (`useMounted`). Debounce primary actions (vote, create, join).

## Strict TypeScript

- No `any`. Type navigation params, API payloads, store state, and component props.
- Reuse existing types from stores / `lib/api.ts` instead of duplicating shapes.
